  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM100#IntervalReading">
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Data captured at regular intervals of time. Interval data could be captured as incremental data, absolute data, or relative data. The source for the data is usually a tariff quantity or an engineering quantity. Data is typically captured in time-tagged, uniform, fixed-length intervals of 5 min, 10 min, 15 min, 30 min, or 60 min. Note: Interval Data is sometimes also called "Interval Data Readings" (IDR).</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61968.ttl" />
